@startuml time_sync_message_flow
title Time Synchronization — BC <-> RT phased message flow (sub-address 1, SystemHandler)\n(NTP four-timestamp; telemetry phase + SYNC_ADJUST; min-delay ClockFilter + OffsetSmoother + smoothed SysTick governor)

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam ParticipantPadding 30

participant "Bus Controller\n(BC host, steady_clock)" as BC
participant "Remote Terminal\n(RT firmware, HAL_GetTick)" as RT

note over BC, RT
  Sync runs as a repeating pair: a TELEMETRY phase of ~10-20 SYNC_PROBE/SYNC_FINAL
  exchanges (measure only), then ONE SYNC_ADJUST that disciplines the SysTick reload.
  PROBE/FINAL payload: [ opcode(1) | units(1) | value(4) ] = 6 bytes; ADJUST: [ opcode(1) ].
  ""units"" is the negative power of ten of the time unit (ms = 3). LE on the wire.
end note

loop ~10-20 exchanges  (TELEMETRY phase — no reload change)

  == Step 1 — SYNC_PROBE (opcode 0x06) ==

  BC -> BC : T1 = clock.now_ms()
  BC -> RT : CMD  sub=1  [ 0x06 | units | T1 (LE) ]
  note right of RT
    RT captures **T2 = clock.now_ms()** immediately on receipt,
    then **T3 = clock.now_ms()** just before replying
    (SyncState::on_probe caches units + T1, stamps T2 and T3).
    T3 - T2 is the RT's own handling time, removed below.
  end note
  RT -> BC : RESP  sub=1  [ T2 | T3 (LE) ]   8-byte payload
  BC -> BC : decode T2, T3; T4 = clock.now_ms()

  == Step 2 — SYNC_FINAL (opcode 0x07) ==

  BC -> RT : CMD  sub=1  [ 0x07 | units | T4 (LE) ]
  note over RT
    **RT collects telemetry (SystemHandler::handle):**
    1. compute_sync_fixed(T1, T2, T3, T4):
         path_delay = ((T4 - T1) - (T3 - T2)) / 2   (one-way, RTT/2)
         offset     = ((T1 - T2) + (T4 - T3)) / 2   (= BC - RT, signed)
    2. ClockFilter::push(T2, offset, path_delay); select():
         pick the LOWEST-delay sample of the last 8 (ties -> newest) -- the
         least jitter-contaminated exchange. A stale-output gate skips
         re-discipline if select() re-returns an already-fed sample.
    3. OffsetSmoother::update(selected anchor, selected offset):
         least-squares fit offset vs local tick over a 32-sample window
         -> intercept = disciplined offset at the anchor
         -> slope     = skew_ppb (BC gain per local ms)
    4. clock.set_bc_discipline(anchor, offset, skew_ppb)   (PATH A only)
         so now_bc_ms() = now_ms + offset + skew*(now-anchor)/1e9
    The SysTick reload is NOT changed here.
  end note
  RT -> BC : RESP  sub=1  16-byte fixed-point result\n[ path_delay_whole | path_delay_frac | offset_whole | offset_frac ]
  note over BC
    Bytes 0..7  : the SELECTED (min-delay) path delay (diagnostic)
    Bytes 8..15 : the **disciplined** offset the RT applied (BC stores it directly)
    The reload is NOT in this reply; it is reported only by SYNC_ADJUST.
  end note

end

== Adjustment — SYNC_ADJUST (opcode 0x08), once per telemetry phase ==

BC -> RT : CMD  sub=1  [ 0x08 ]
note over RT
  **RT applies one smoothed reload step (PATH B):**
    avg_skew_ppb = phase_anchor.adjust_skew_ppb()   (long-baseline average;
      falls back to the windowed clock.bc_skew_ppb() before the first baseline)
    reload = next_tick_reload(current, nominal, avg_skew_ppb):
      move gain (3/4) of the way to round(current*(1 - skew/1e9)),
      clamp to +/-10% of nominal; |skew| < 6000 ppb deadband -> no-op
    if reload changed: set_tick_reload() writes SysTick->LOAD directly
      (VAL preserved, no time bled); the rate change is propagated back
      into Path A (anchor dropped, smoother window rebased)
end note
RT -> BC : RESP  sub=1  8-byte result\n[ avg_skew_ppb (i32) | reload (u32) ]

note over BC, RT
  Repeat the pair. Each phase measures the residual skew at the new rate and the
  next adjust steps less, so the clocks lock over several cycles. RtClient does no
  BC-side filtering: clock_offset_units()/reload_ticks() mirror the RT exactly.
end note

@enduml
